1
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:11,546
<font color="#4096d1"> -==www.RagBear.com==- 是, 首相  第2季第5集

2
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,747
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:29,662
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译: 多切 校对: Tpring 时间轴: 褪色の蓝

4
00:00:35,534 --> 00:00:39,062
还政于民

5
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:43,689
早安 伯纳      早安 首相
Morning.          Morning.

6
00:00:43,858 --> 00:00:46,217
您要在5分钟内去电视摄影棚
You have to leave for the TV studiosin five minutes.

7
00:00:46,218 --> 00:00:47,168
我准备好了
I'm ready.

8
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:49,438
您还记得访谈的内容吗?
Do you remember what the interview's about?

9
00:00:49,974 --> 00:00:51,650
地方政府
Local government.

10
00:00:51,818 --> 00:00:54,013
唯一一件我无处下手的事
The one thing I can do nothing about.

11
00:00:54,178 --> 00:00:57,462
这些可恶的政务委员会 都由一群腐败的
These wretched councils are run by a bunch of corrupt morons

12
00:00:57,463 --> 00:00:58,837
耍小聪明的白痴管理
who are too clever by half.

13
00:00:58,838 --> 00:01:01,790
有小聪明就不叫白痴了
The most a moron can be is less clever by half.

14
00:01:01,791 --> 00:01:04,496
这些委员不都是民主选举出来的吗?
These councillors are democratically elected.

15
00:01:04,658 --> 00:01:06,151
那要看你怎么定义"民主"了
Depends how you define democracy.

16
00:01:06,152 --> 00:01:09,448
只有约25%的人在地方选举时投了票
Only about 25% of people vote in a local election.

17
00:01:09,618 --> 00:01:12,015
投票也只把它当成支持率调查
Those who do regard it as a popularity pole

18
00:01:12,016 --> 00:01:13,896
给中央政府做参考的
for the real leaders in Westminster.

19
00:01:14,058 --> 00:01:16,554
但那些地方委员也还是民意代表
But councillors are still representatives.

20
00:01:16,555 --> 00:01:18,256
他们代表谁呀?
Who do they represent?

21
00:01:18,418 --> 00:01:20,963
没人知道自己的委员是谁
Nobody knows who their councillor is.

22
00:01:20,964 --> 00:01:22,172
你知道你的委员是谁吗?
Do you know who yours is?

23
00:01:22,338 --> 00:01:25,057
不知道          你当然不会知道
No.        Well, no, of course you don't.

24
00:01:25,218 --> 00:01:27,209
那些委员也都清楚
The councillors know this,

25
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,694
所以他们4年都胡来一气
so they spend four totally unaccountable years

26
00:01:29,695 --> 00:01:32,168
拿着公款沽名钓誉
on a publicly subsidised ego trip.

27
00:01:32,338 --> 00:01:35,887
他们扰乱内城区 把学校搞垮
They ruin the inner cities, let the schools fall to bits,

28
00:01:36,058 --> 00:01:38,458
打击警察士气 削弱法律权威
they demoralise the police and undermine law and order,

29
00:01:38,459 --> 00:01:40,051
最后就来怪我
then blame me.

30
00:01:40,858 --> 00:01:44,328
您要这么说吗?          没听到我刚说了吗?
Will you say that? I've just said it. Didn't you hear me?

31
00:01:45,178 --> 00:01:46,260
不 我是说在电视上
No, I mean on television.

32
00:01:46,261 --> 00:01:49,888
当然不会 那样显得我没肚量
Of course not. It'd make me sound intolerant.

33
00:01:50,898 --> 00:01:53,696
豪兹维斯区委员长 该死的艾格尼丝-莫豪
Houndsworth Council leader, Agnes Moorhouse,

34
00:01:53,858 --> 00:01:56,058
威胁要扣留给警察的拨款
threatens to withhold police funds

35
00:01:56,059 --> 00:01:57,567
并禁止他们使用政府房产
and ban them from council property.

36
00:01:57,738 --> 00:02:01,048
她不能这样 1964年警务法案第5条规定
She can't do that. Section 5 of the Police Act, 1964.

37
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:04,608
"区政府必须保质保量提供警力" 上面写着
Councils must provide an adequate and efficient police force.

38
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:07,584
她说除非警员队伍有50%黑人
She says that until the police force is 50% black,

39
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,488
否则既不够质 也不够量
it can't be adequate or efficient.

40
00:02:10,378 --> 00:02:14,166
她怎么证明          不幸的是 她治下的警察
She can't prove that.        Unfortunately, her own police force

41
00:02:14,338 --> 00:02:17,728
无论质和量 在全国都排倒数第一
is the most inadequate and least efficient in the country.

42
00:02:17,898 --> 00:02:21,288
大家都担心上了法庭 她能证明出来
Everybody's terrified that she will prove it.

43
00:02:22,418 --> 00:02:26,013
汉弗莱 我们得对这个莫豪有所动作
Humphrey, we've got to do something about Agnes Moorhouse.

44
00:02:26,178 --> 00:02:29,170
她的辖区已经完全成了禁区      的确
Her borough's practically a no go area.        Indeed.

45
00:02:29,338 --> 00:02:32,569
现在怎么办?      写封措词严厉的信如何?
What?        How about a strongly worded letter?

46
00:02:32,738 --> 00:02:34,962
然后收到一封措词更严厉的信
And get a more strongly worded letter in reply,

47
00:02:34,963 --> 00:02:37,937
还抄送给报社? 这不是自找麻烦吗
copied to the newspapers? Asking for trouble.

48
00:02:38,098 --> 00:02:41,408
拿法律对付她?          她是个律师
Draw her attention to the law.        She is a lawyer.

49
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:44,326
钻法律空子正是她的看家本领
Getting round the law is what she's paid for.

50
00:02:44,327 --> 00:02:46,257
那干脆不理她?
Why not just ignore her?

51
00:02:46,258 --> 00:02:49,101
让大家说我把市镇控制权拱手让给
Have everyone say I'd handed over control of the inner cities

52
00:02:49,102 --> 00:02:50,968
那些激进分子吗?
to the militant loonies?

53
00:02:51,138 --> 00:02:54,757
这女人是个疯子 汉弗莱
She's a wild woman, Humphrey.

54
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:55,973
不 必须得有人跟她谈谈
No, someone's got to have a word with her.

55
00:02:56,138 --> 00:02:59,210
讲讲安全问题      检察官?
Point out the security implications.        A law officer?

56
00:02:59,378 --> 00:03:02,848
不 不能是政治对抗 必须是行政人员
No. Can't be a political confrontation. Has to be an official.

57
00:03:03,018 --> 00:03:07,330
必须是负责保安事务的人
Somebody with responsibility for security.

58
00:03:07,498 --> 00:03:10,376
必须是负责...
Somebody with responsibility...

59
00:03:11,018 --> 00:03:15,330
不不 首相 不行 她是个大怪兽
No, no, no, no, Prime Minister, no! She's a monster!

60
00:03:15,498 --> 00:03:19,082
不不 这事归警察厅 内政部
No, i i it's up to Scotland Yard, the Home Office,

61
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:23,069
安全局...我是说特工局....军情五处
the Security Branch, er, Special Branch, I mean, the...the Ml5,

62
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:25,734
大法官 环境部...
the Lord Chancellor, Department of the Environment...

63
00:03:25,898 --> 00:03:28,970
白鳕鱼管理局?      白鳕鱼...不不
The White Fish Authority?      White Fish... No, no, no!

64
00:03:29,138 --> 00:03:31,623
安全部门不是你负责的吗
Don't you coordinate the security services?

65
00:03:31,624 --> 00:03:32,335
是 是
Yes, yes...

66
00:03:32,498 --> 00:03:35,259
或者我们该换个人来负责?
Or should we give that job to someone else?

67
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,208
不 不 不
No, no, no, no, no.

68
00:03:37,378 --> 00:03:39,656
就这么定了 去跟她私下谈谈
That's agreed, then. A quiet word.

69
00:03:39,657 --> 00:03:41,417
达成君子协议
Come to a gentlemen's agreement.

70
00:03:41,578 --> 00:03:43,773
可她不是君子
But she's not a gentleman!

71
00:03:43,938 --> 00:03:45,929
她连淑女都算不上
She's not even a lady!

72
00:03:46,938 --> 00:03:50,089
我要你来对付她 走吧 伯纳
I want YOU to handle her. Come on.

73
00:03:51,338 --> 00:03:53,135
对付她?
Handle her?

74
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:56,468
进来
Come in.

75
00:03:57,658 --> 00:04:01,446
艾格尼丝-莫豪来了 汉弗莱爵士          好吧
Agnes Moorhouse to see you, Sir Humphrey.        Right.

76
00:04:04,738 --> 00:04:07,415
亲爱的女士 见到你真高兴
Oh, my dear lady, how very nice to meet you.

77
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:10,813
请进 坐这边好吗?
Come in. Won't you come and sit down? Now...

78
00:04:12,738 --> 00:04:16,520
好吧 能不能帮莫豪小姐倒杯茶?
Um... right... Would you get Miss Moorhouse a cup of tea.

79
00:04:16,521 --> 00:04:19,097
或者是莫豪夫人?
Or is it Mrs Moorhouse?

80
00:04:19,098 --> 00:04:22,488
你很关心我的婚姻状况吗?          不不
Is my marital status really your concern?        Er, no, no.

81
00:04:22,658 --> 00:04:23,840
只是...你知道
It's just... You know,

82
00:04:23,841 --> 00:04:26,412
我只是担心 呃...
I was just... worried about whether the... er...

83
00:04:26,578 --> 00:04:29,570
呃 你能...帮她倒杯茶吗?
Er, would you get... her a cup of tea?

84
00:04:31,578 --> 00:04:34,112
我该怎么称呼你呢 莫豪小姐吗
What should I call you? Ms Moorhouse?

85
00:04:34,113 --> 00:04:36,413
叫我艾格尼丝 我该怎么叫你
Call me Agnes. What shall I call you?

86
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:41,297
你可以叫我汉弗莱爵士
...well, you can call me Sir Humphrey.

87
00:04:41,458 --> 00:04:43,449
那么 亲爱的女士
Now, my dear lady...

88
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:46,542
我不是你"亲爱的女士"
I'm not your "dear lady".

89
00:04:46,543 --> 00:04:49,134
少来这套伪绅士的废话了 好吗?
Don't patronise me and cut out the sexist crap, OK?

90
00:04:52,738 --> 00:04:54,968
好吧 艾格尼丝
Er... OK, Agnes.

91
00:04:55,138 --> 00:04:58,414
我约你见面是觉得 我们该交流一下
I wanted us to have this meeting so we could try

92
00:04:58,415 --> 00:04:59,529
促进共识
and understand one another.

93
00:04:59,698 --> 00:05:02,132
这当然是不谋而合的          是吗?
I'm sure we're in agreement.        Really?

94
00:05:02,298 --> 00:05:05,495
显然 你对治理国家有自己的一套
You have your own views about how Britain should be run,

95
00:05:05,658 --> 00:05:08,100
但我相信我们俩都同意 根本上要
but I'm sure we agree on a fundamental basis

96
00:05:08,101 --> 00:05:09,207
保证秩序和政府权威
of order and authority.

97
00:05:09,378 --> 00:05:11,812
说对一半      一半?
That's half true.      Half true?

98
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:15,414
你同意 我不同意          可这很明显啊
You agree, I don't.        But it's obvious!

99
00:05:15,578 --> 00:05:17,751
很明显 你用现行体制立了法
if you've got it made under this system,

100
00:05:17,752 --> 00:05:20,777
是想用政府权威维护你的特权
you use authority to preserve your privileges.

101
00:05:20,938 --> 00:05:24,328
可那些流浪汉 失业者和穷人呢?
What about the homeless, the unemployed, the poor?

102
00:05:24,498 --> 00:05:26,454
艾格尼丝 我了解他们
I know all about them.

103
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:29,815
真的 你了解什么?
Really? What do you know?

104
00:05:29,978 --> 00:05:31,735
我看过所有发表的报告
I've read all the published papers.

105
00:05:31,736 --> 00:05:34,369
所有统计数据 所有官方汇报
I've seen all the statistics.

106
00:05:34,538 --> 00:05:37,575
相信我 亲爱的女士...艾格尼丝 我...
Believe me, dear lady... Agnes, I... I...

107
00:05:38,938 --> 00:05:41,930
我真的了解他们      好呀
I do know all about them.      Fine.

108
00:05:42,098 --> 00:05:45,090
半磅黄油要多少钱?
What does half a pound of margarine cost?

109
00:05:45,898 --> 00:05:49,493
什么?      半磅黄油要多少钱?
What?       What does half a pound of margarine cost?

110
00:05:49,658 --> 00:05:52,092
呃 我怎么知道...2毛
Oh... er... How should I know? Er... 20p.

111
00:05:52,258 --> 00:05:56,331
2毛?      2块4吧 我不知道
20p?!      2.40! I don't know!

112
00:05:56,498 --> 00:05:58,904
就是 你怎么会知道?
Right. Why should you?

113
00:05:58,905 --> 00:06:00,696
社保局几点开门呢?
What time do Social Security offices open?

114
00:06:03,018 --> 00:06:05,202
一台单杠式取暖器
How long can you run a one bar fire

115
00:06:05,203 --> 00:06:06,533
5毛钱可以跳多少表?
with 50 pence in the meter?

116
00:06:06,698 --> 00:06:08,689
我不太明白你在说什么
I'm not entirely sure I follow.

117
00:06:08,858 --> 00:06:11,157
你当然不知道 如果你知道
If you knew that,

118
00:06:11,158 --> 00:06:13,886
你就不会同意用政府来支撑制度
you wouldn't agree about using authority to support the system.

119
00:06:14,058 --> 00:06:18,529
我能理解 我也同情 帮人脱贫功德无量啊
I do understand. I do sympathise.

120
00:06:18,698 --> 00:06:21,535
但我们真的没有资源来实现
But we haven't the resources to achieve that.

121
00:06:21,536 --> 00:06:22,168
谁没有?
Who hasn't?

122
00:06:22,338 --> 00:06:25,330
国家      真的吗?
The nation.        Really?

123
00:06:26,858 --> 00:06:30,851
这张桌子是国家的吗? 这件陶瓷?
Does this desk belong to the nation? This china?

124
00:06:31,018 --> 00:06:34,055
是白瓷      白瓷
Porcelain.      Porcelain.

125
00:06:34,218 --> 00:06:37,358
这些画是国家的? 要么是你私人的?
These portraits? Or are they your own?

126
00:06:37,359 --> 00:06:39,008
这些是政府财产
They're government property.

127
00:06:39,178 --> 00:06:42,773
很好 这些东西可以卖...差不多8万吧?
Oh, good. They should fetch about   what?   80,000.

128
00:06:42,938 --> 00:06:45,755
足够20个单亲家庭过1年了
That'll keep 20 one parent families for a year.

129
00:06:45,756 --> 00:06:46,897
你的工资呢?
What about your salary?

130
00:06:47,058 --> 00:06:48,582
这与此无关
That has nothing to do with it!

131
00:06:48,583 --> 00:06:51,449
很好 也一起划过来
Good, then we'll have that, too.

132
00:06:51,618 --> 00:06:55,213
给你每周100元 又给需要的人每年省出7万
Leave you ?00 a week. That's 70,000 a year for the needy.

133
00:06:55,378 --> 00:06:59,496
我的工资是经济综合结构的一部分
My salary is merely part of a complex economic structure.

134
00:06:59,658 --> 00:07:01,455
好呀 我们把它简单化
We'll simplify it.

135
00:07:01,618 --> 00:07:03,779
毕竟 你也不是为了发财
After all, you don't want to make a profit

136
00:07:03,779 --> 00:07:06,533
才为国效力的 对吧?
out of serving your country, do you?

137
00:07:09,858 --> 00:07:11,655
啊 茶来了
Ah, tea.

138
00:07:12,498 --> 00:07:15,217
这边 艾琳
Over here, Eileen. Um...

139
00:07:15,378 --> 00:07:18,973
太好了 非常感谢 要我做东道吗?
How very nice. Thank you so much. Shall I be mother?

140
00:07:24,538 --> 00:07:27,416
告诉我 艾格尼丝
Tell me, um... Agnes...

141
00:07:27,578 --> 00:07:32,398
你有一条政策 你辖区内只允许出售
...this policy of yours of only allowing free range eggs

142
00:07:32,398 --> 00:07:35,770
放养鸡下的蛋 这能改善贫困吗?
to be sold in your borough, how does this help poverty?

143
00:07:35,938 --> 00:07:39,407
动物也有权利 懂吗
Animals have rights too, you know.

144
00:07:39,408 --> 00:07:41,251
圈养鸡一辈子生不如死
A battery chicken's life isn't worth living.

145
00:07:41,418 --> 00:07:43,137
你愿意一辈子跟600名
Would you want to spend your life packed in

146
00:07:43,138 --> 00:07:46,253
吵吵闹闹 臭烘烘的生灵挤在一起吗?
with 600 other squawking, smelly creatures,

147
00:07:46,418 --> 00:07:48,533
无法呼吸新鲜空气 无法移动
unable to breathe fresh air, unable to move,

148
00:07:48,534 --> 00:07:50,206
无法伸展 无法思考?
unable to think?

149
00:07:50,378 --> 00:07:50,625
当然不愿意
Certainly not.

150
00:07:50,626 --> 00:07:54,132
所以我从不参选议员
That's why I never stood for Parliament.

151
00:07:55,618 --> 00:07:57,415
要糖吗?      不用 谢谢
Sugar?        No, thank you.

152
00:07:57,578 --> 00:08:01,776
好 谈谈警察问题吧
Now, let's turn to this matter of the police.

153
00:08:01,938 --> 00:08:04,516
你想要扣留警察的拨款
You want to withhold funds from the police,

154
00:08:04,517 --> 00:08:07,012
禁止他们使用政府房产
ban them from council property,

155
00:08:07,178 --> 00:08:10,966
解雇警察局长 再设立一些禁区
sack the Chief Constable, and allow several no go areas.

156
00:08:11,138 --> 00:08:14,847
没错        但你难道不明白
That's it.        But can't you see

157
00:08:15,018 --> 00:08:19,728
充足的警力对我们大家都有好处?
that an adequate police enforcement is in all our interests?

158
00:08:19,898 --> 00:08:22,804
尤其能照顾到那些贫困的
And it is especially in the interestsof all those poor,

159
00:08:22,804 --> 00:08:28,050
住在高犯罪率区域的平民
ordinary folk who dwell in the high crime housing estates.

160
00:08:28,218 --> 00:08:30,527
恕难苟同
I don't accept that.

161
00:08:30,698 --> 00:08:32,625
你想让他们处在被抢劫 强奸
Oh, you want them to be in danger of being mugged

162
00:08:32,626 --> 00:08:34,771
被土炸弹炸死的危险当中吗
and raped and bombed?

163
00:08:34,938 --> 00:08:36,738
这是没有办法的事
Can't be helped.

164
00:08:36,739 --> 00:08:38,135
可这会最终颠覆
But this could lead to the overthrow

165
00:08:38,298 --> 00:08:41,030
我们的政府体制 我们的整个生活方式
of our system of government, our way of life!

166
00:08:41,031 --> 00:08:42,689
是你的 不是他们的
Yours, not theirs.

167
00:08:42,858 --> 00:08:45,850
那么 你乐意把议会废除掉?        是的
You would be happy to abolish Parliament?      Yes.

168
00:08:46,018 --> 00:08:47,815
还有法院?        是的
The courts?      Yes.

169
00:08:47,978 --> 00:08:50,538
君主制呢?        当然了
The monarchy?!      Of course.

170
00:08:51,538 --> 00:08:55,612
既然你在兴头上 还想烧了我的办公室吧
Perhaps you'd like to burn down my office!

171
00:08:55,613 --> 00:08:56,692
火柴在这里
That matches are over here!

172
00:08:56,858 --> 00:08:59,372
不 当然不想了         为什么?
No, certainly not.          Why?

173
00:09:00,698 --> 00:09:02,689
也许我用得上
I may need it.

174
00:09:05,018 --> 00:09:08,293
你知道那个女人艾格尼斯-莫豪吗?        怎么?
You know that Agnes Moorhouse woman?        Yes?

175
00:09:08,458 --> 00:09:10,247
我让汉弗莱去找她谈谈
I told Humphrey to have a word with her.

176
00:09:10,248 --> 00:09:12,736
有趣的尝试
Interesting experiment.

177
00:09:12,898 --> 00:09:15,951
他说谈得不错 但又不愿多说
He says it went well, but he didn't want to talk about it

178
00:09:15,951 --> 00:09:18,280
只在10分钟里干掉了4大杯威士忌
and had four whiskies in ten minutes.

179
00:09:18,738 --> 00:09:20,933
这些地方政府怎么回事?
What is it about local government?

180
00:09:21,098 --> 00:09:23,733
我刚跟市政厅闹了一场
I've had trouble with the town hall.

181
00:09:23,734 --> 00:09:26,092
他们把老年人圣诞派对取消了
They've cancelled the old people's Christmas party.

182
00:09:26,258 --> 00:09:30,137
为什么?        跟新员工加班协议有关
Why?          New staff overtime agreements.

183
00:09:30,298 --> 00:09:31,393
"都是你丈夫的错 哈克夫人"
"It's your husband's fault.

184
00:09:31,393 --> 00:09:33,067
"你让他给我们钱"
Tell him to give us the money"

185
00:09:33,067 --> 00:09:34,769
"就让你们开派对"
"and you can have the party."

186
00:09:34,938 --> 00:09:37,751
好呀 全国所有市政厅的所有蠢事
Every piece of stupidity and incompetence

187
00:09:37,752 --> 00:09:39,932
和不作为行为都怪在我身上
in every town hall in Britain is blamed on me.

188
00:09:40,098 --> 00:09:42,089
准是多萝西
That'll be Dorothy.

189
00:09:42,258 --> 00:09:45,555
我叫她过来谈谈这件事
I asked her up here to have a word about that very thing.

190
00:09:45,556 --> 00:09:48,049
多萝西 进来吧
Dorothy, come in.

191
00:09:48,218 --> 00:09:50,205
过来坐吧
Come and sit down.

192
00:09:50,206 --> 00:09:53,212
你告诉我 地方政府到底什么毛病?
Now, tell me, what is wrong with local government?

193
00:09:53,378 --> 00:09:56,051
嗯 这是种非敌既我的状况
Well, it's a them and us situation.

194
00:09:56,218 --> 00:09:58,128
地方执政者应该是我们
The local authority ought to be us.

195
00:09:58,129 --> 00:10:00,211
我们人民 还是我们中央政府?
Us the people or us the government?

196
00:10:00,378 --> 00:10:03,002
在民主制度下 应该是一样的啊
In a democracy that ought to be the same thing.

197
00:10:03,003 --> 00:10:04,371
我们都知道不是的
We all know it isn't.

198
00:10:04,538 --> 00:10:06,103
不 我是说我们人民
I mean us, the people.

199
00:10:06,104 --> 00:10:09,798
应该服务我们 是我们一份子 可他们不是
They ought to be running things for us.

200
00:10:09,799 --> 00:10:11,283
只为他们自己做事
But they're running things for them.

201
00:10:11,284 --> 00:10:14,091
为他们的权力 便利和利益
For their power, their convenience and their benefit.

202
00:10:14,258 --> 00:10:16,726
这我知道        那该怎么办
I know that.          So what's the answer?

203
00:10:16,898 --> 00:10:19,935
对抗他们        不 让他们变成我们
Fight them.        No. Make them us.

204
00:10:20,098 --> 00:10:20,857
怎么说?
How do you mean?

205
00:10:20,858 --> 00:10:23,727
假设你要阻止一个大型政府项目 你怎么办?
How do you stop a major government project?

206
00:10:23,898 --> 00:10:25,889
找公务员配合
Join the Civil Service.

207
00:10:27,138 --> 00:10:29,174
不 我是说如果你是个普通人
If you're an ordinary person.

208
00:10:29,338 --> 00:10:32,480
我不记得当平民是什么感觉了
I can't remember what that was like.

209
00:10:32,481 --> 00:10:34,571
照民意测验来看 你就快知道了
Judging from opinion polls, you'll soon find out.

210
00:10:34,738 --> 00:10:37,432
想象你是个平头百姓 吉姆
Just imagine you're an ordinary person, Jim.

211
00:10:37,433 --> 00:10:38,970
好 我试试
Well, I'll try.

212
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:41,732
假设要扩宽道路 或者建机场
Imagine you want to stop a road widening scheme

213
00:10:41,733 --> 00:10:44,337
要拆迁你的房子 你会怎么办?
or an airport being built. What do you do?

214
00:10:44,498 --> 00:10:47,058
给你的议会代表写信        这有用吗?
Write to your MP.        That does the trick?

215
00:10:47,218 --> 00:10:49,908
当然没用 可普通人就是这么做的
Of course not, but that's what ordinary people do

216
00:10:49,909 --> 00:10:51,848
因为普通人都是笨蛋
'cause ordinary people are stupid.

217
00:10:52,018 --> 00:10:53,575
这就是为什么他们选你吧?
Is that why they elected you?

218
00:10:53,576 --> 00:10:55,806
别拆我台 亲爱的 谢谢
Stop barracking, darling, please.

219
00:10:55,978 --> 00:10:58,776
我正试着理解多萝西的见解呢
I'm trying to understand what Dorothy's driving at.

220
00:10:58,938 --> 00:11:00,797
普通人会组成一个组织
Ordinary people form a group

221
00:11:00,798 --> 00:11:03,090
来与不利的官方计划对抗
to fight official plans they don't want

222
00:11:03,258 --> 00:11:05,977
由这个组织代表所有当地人
and this group represents the local people.

223
00:11:06,138 --> 00:11:08,936
它跟地方政府不一样
This group is different from the local authority

224
00:11:09,098 --> 00:11:11,941
因为地方政府并不代表
because the local authority doesn't really represent

225
00:11:11,942 --> 00:11:13,925
当地人民        为什么?
the local people.          Why not?

226
00:11:13,926 --> 00:11:17,209
因为政务委员都是地方小团体人士
Councillors are all drawn from tiny local parties.

227
00:11:17,578 --> 00:11:20,583
当一个社区真的重视某个问题
When a local community really cares about an issue,

228
00:11:20,584 --> 00:11:23,241
他们组成一个委员会 然后上街
they form a committee, and then they talk to people

229
00:11:23,241 --> 00:11:25,931
去超市 或挨家挨户游说
in the supermarkets and on the doorstep.

230
00:11:26,098 --> 00:11:28,532
争取支持 争取资金
They drum up support and raise money.

231
00:11:28,698 --> 00:11:30,625
而这些钱跟政府收费不同
And this money isn't like the rates.

232
00:11:30,626 --> 00:11:34,091
它们会被用在人们希望用的地方
It's spent on what people actually want it spent on.

233
00:11:34,258 --> 00:11:36,462
我打赌本地的百姓都乐意
I bet ordinary people would like

234
00:11:36,462 --> 00:11:38,410
让老年人开个圣诞派对
the old folks to have a Christmas party.

235
00:11:38,578 --> 00:11:41,376
当然 可市政厅宁愿要幢新大楼
The town hall would rather have a new town hall

236
00:11:41,538 --> 00:11:45,053
或者让委员们去巴哈马岛公费考察
or a councillors' fact finding mission to the Bahamas.

237
00:11:45,218 --> 00:11:48,528
那该怎么办?      很明显呀 废除他们
What do you do?        It's obvious. Abolish them.

238
00:11:48,698 --> 00:11:51,496
把权力都揽到中央政府
Invest all power in the central government.

239
00:11:51,658 --> 00:11:55,412
这正是汉弗莱的主张        是吧 什么?
That's exactly what Humphrey would say.        See? What?

240
00:11:55,578 --> 00:11:58,061
吉姆 你完全没领会
Jim, you've completely missed the point

241
00:11:58,062 --> 00:11:59,776
我说的意思啊
of everything I've been saying.

242
00:11:59,938 --> 00:12:02,980
我的意思是要还政于民
The idea is to return power to ordinary people

243
00:12:02,981 --> 00:12:05,570
而不让市政机器霸占
and take it away from the town hall machine.

244
00:12:05,738 --> 00:12:08,553
使得地方政府真正负起责任来
Make local government genuinely accountable.

245
00:12:08,554 --> 00:12:09,413
对 可怎么做?
Yes, but how?

246
00:12:09,578 --> 00:12:12,565
本月<政治评论>上有篇文章规划好了
It's all in an article in this month's "Political Review"

247
00:12:12,566 --> 00:12:13,890
作者叫马里奥教授
by Professor Marriott.

248
00:12:14,058 --> 00:12:16,856
办法是 多多设立小选区
Now, you create little voting districts.

249
00:12:17,018 --> 00:12:19,192
每200户人家选出
200 or so households electing

250
00:12:19,193 --> 00:12:22,012
自己的行政委员会 化城为村
their own little parish council, a city village.

251
00:12:22,178 --> 00:12:25,038
这个行政委员会的主席
The chairman of this little parish council

252
00:12:25,039 --> 00:12:27,730
就是他们在地方政府中的代表
is their representative on the local authority.

253
00:12:27,898 --> 00:12:30,856
那每个镇区就有500个委员了
You'd have about 500 councillors to each borough.

254
00:12:31,018 --> 00:12:34,215
没错 然后他们再选出个执行委员会
That's right. So they'd elect an executive council.

255
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:37,768
这样地方政府就有了议会和内阁
The local authority would have a parliament and a cabinet.

256
00:12:37,938 --> 00:12:41,135
不能让议会选内阁 不能这样
Parliament don't elect the Cabinet. We don't want that.

257
00:12:41,298 --> 00:12:43,901
这样参与性就强过头了
That'd be taking participation to extreme lengths.

258
00:12:43,902 --> 00:12:45,610
这些委员会就这样
These councils would.

259
00:12:45,778 --> 00:12:49,391
每一个议员就能与他左邻右舍
Each councillor would be in door to door contact

260
00:12:49,392 --> 00:12:51,011
选他的人保持紧密联系
with the people who voted for him.

261
00:12:51,178 --> 00:12:55,649
多萝西 这简直是1832年议会改革法案
Dorothy, this could be like the Great Reform Act of 1832.

262
00:12:55,818 --> 00:12:58,730
这些委员会就像当年的不平等选区
These councils are like old rotten boroughs.

263
00:12:58,898 --> 00:13:00,686
六七个人就可以决定
Half a dozen people deciding

264
00:13:00,687 --> 00:13:03,050
未来4年市政厅的领导
who'll be in the town hall for the next four years.

265
00:13:03,218 --> 00:13:06,654
没错        而伟大的改革家就是我
Precisely.      And I shall be the great reformer!

266
00:13:08,018 --> 00:13:11,010
<哈克改革法案> 应该由我亲自颁布
Hacker's Reform Bill. I shall introduce it myself.

267
00:13:12,178 --> 00:13:13,743
这个国家的权力不出自
The power of this country does not lie in

268
00:13:13,744 --> 00:13:17,880
办公室和机关 它出自每个英国子民
offices and institutions, it lies in the stout hearts

269
00:13:17,881 --> 00:13:21,258
坚强的意志和心灵之中
and strong wills of the yeomen of Britain!

270
00:13:21,418 --> 00:13:24,216
女人也投票啊
Women have the vote, too!

271
00:13:24,378 --> 00:13:26,369
还有英国女子民
The yeowomen of Britain.

272
00:13:27,378 --> 00:13:30,176
平民 平头百姓? 不行
Yeopersons. Yeopeople? No.

273
00:13:30,338 --> 00:13:33,136
这个岛国的人民
...the people of this island race.

274
00:13:33,298 --> 00:13:35,493
他们宽厚而睿智的肩膀...
On their broad and wise shoulders...

275
00:13:35,658 --> 00:13:37,694
肩膀怎么能睿智呢
You can't have wise shoulders.

276
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:43,091
他们宽厚的肩膀和睿智的心灵...头脑
On their broad shoulders and wise hearts... heads...

277
00:13:43,258 --> 00:13:46,568
我们的未来 蕴藏在他们睿智的头脑中
In their wise heads lies our destiny.

278
00:13:46,738 --> 00:13:49,536
我们必须还政于民
We must give back power to the people!

279
00:13:49,698 --> 00:13:53,008
我应当亲自颁布这个...
And I shall be the one to introduce this... um...

280
00:13:53,178 --> 00:13:55,328
这个新计划取什么名呢?
What shall I call this new scheme?

281
00:13:55,498 --> 00:13:57,648
民主?
Democracy?

282
00:14:00,193 --> 00:14:01,403
请进
YES

283
00:14:01,518 --> 00:14:05,010
汉弗莱爵士 您找我?        是的 伯纳
You wanted to see me?        Oh, yes, Bernard.

284
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,766
伯纳 我想跟你谈谈
Bernard, I want to have a word with you

285
00:14:07,767 --> 00:14:09,649
马里奥教授的文章
about Professor Marriott's article.

286
00:14:09,818 --> 00:14:12,164
对 我觉得地方政府是该改革了
I think it's time we reformed local government.

287
00:14:12,165 --> 00:14:13,015
是吗 伯纳?
Do you?

288
00:14:13,178 --> 00:14:14,975
是的
Yes.

289
00:14:17,258 --> 00:14:19,249
至少 我觉得我同意
At least I think I did.

290
00:14:20,498 --> 00:14:23,092
就是说 我并不是太反对
That is, I'm not wholly against it.

291
00:14:24,098 --> 00:14:27,026
尽管也有很多...有力的
Although there are many... convincing,

292
00:14:27,027 --> 00:14:30,128
有人认为很有见地的反对意见
some might say conclusive, arguments against it.

293
00:14:30,298 --> 00:14:32,687
确实是有人 伯纳
Some might indeed, Bernard.

294
00:14:32,858 --> 00:14:34,610
对 为什么
Yes. Why?

295
00:14:34,778 --> 00:14:36,848
伯纳 因为一旦你开创了
Because once you create

296
00:14:37,018 --> 00:14:41,409
真正民主的地方社区 就不会到此为止
genuinely democratic local communities, it won't stop there.

297
00:14:41,578 --> 00:14:44,615
不会吗?      当然不会
Won't it?      Well, of course it won't.

298
00:14:44,778 --> 00:14:47,604
你想想 这些机构一旦成立
You see, once they get established,

299
00:14:47,605 --> 00:14:49,977
他们必将争取更大权力
they'll insist on more power.

300
00:14:50,138 --> 00:14:52,592
政治家们将不敢不放权
Politicians will be too frightened to withhold them,

301
00:14:52,593 --> 00:14:54,893
于是就形成了地区小政府
so you'll get regional government.

302
00:14:55,058 --> 00:14:59,051
这有问题吗?      伯纳 过来坐下
Would that matter?      Bernard, come and sit down.

303
00:15:00,338 --> 00:15:02,005
伯纳 假设今时今日
What happens at the moment if there is

304
00:15:02,006 --> 00:15:05,048
在诺丁汉有了一块空地
some vacant land in, say, Nottingham

305
00:15:05,218 --> 00:15:07,429
有几个方案争着要用它
and there are rival proposals for its use

306
00:15:07,430 --> 00:15:09,177
要建医院 学校或机场呢?
hospital, college, airport?

307
00:15:09,338 --> 00:15:11,503
我们设一个部门联席委员会
We set up an inter departmental committee.

308
00:15:11,504 --> 00:15:15,527
卫生部 教育部 交通部 环境部
Health, Education, Transport, Environment.

309
00:15:15,698 --> 00:15:17,732
要求他们打报告 开些会 交提案
Ask for papers, hold meetings, propose,

310
00:15:17,733 --> 00:15:20,249
讨论 修正 再打报告 重拟提案
discuss, revise, report back, re draft.

311
00:15:20,418 --> 00:15:23,808
非常正确 数个月卓有成效的工作
Precisely. Months of fruitful work.

312
00:15:25,738 --> 00:15:28,730
最终达成一个成熟且负责任的结论
Leading to a mature and responsible conclusion.

313
00:15:28,898 --> 00:15:30,856
但如果有个地区政府
But if you have regional government,

314
00:15:30,857 --> 00:15:33,289
他们在诺丁汉就可以决定
they decide it all in Nottingham!

315
00:15:33,458 --> 00:15:37,246
也许开几个会就完了 相当地不专业
Probably in a couple of meetings! Complete amateurs!

316
00:15:37,418 --> 00:15:40,649
可那是他们的地区        那我们怎么办?
It is their city.        And what happens to us?

317
00:15:40,818 --> 00:15:42,075
工作量大幅减少
Well, much less work.

318
00:15:42,076 --> 00:15:44,199
对 工作量大幅减少
Yes, much less work!

319
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:48,366
少到几个大臣自己就能完成了
So little that ministers might be able to do it on their own,

320
00:15:48,367 --> 00:15:50,610
我们会失去很多的权力
so we'd have much less power!

321
00:15:51,298 --> 00:15:53,334
我不确定我想不想要权力
I don't know if I want power.

322
00:15:53,498 --> 00:15:56,093
伯纳德 如果该掌权的人不掌权
If the right people don't have power,

323
00:15:56,094 --> 00:15:57,093
你知道会怎样吗?
know what happens?

324
00:15:57,258 --> 00:15:59,249
不该掌的人就掌权了
The wrong people get it!

325
00:16:00,658 --> 00:16:05,012
政客们 委员们 普通选民们
Politicians, councillors, ordinary voters!

326
00:16:05,013 --> 00:16:07,097
但在民主制度下 这不是天经地义吗?
But aren't they supposed to in a democracy?

327
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:12,048
我们是英式民主 伯纳          这怎么说?
This is a British democracy, Bernard!        How do you mean?

328
00:16:12,218 --> 00:16:16,052
英式民主认为 我们需要有个体制
British democracy recognises that you need a system

329
00:16:16,218 --> 00:16:18,686
保护生活中重要的东西
to protect the important things of life

330
00:16:18,858 --> 00:16:22,248
保证它们不落到化外之民手上
and keep them out of the hands of the barbarians!

331
00:16:24,378 --> 00:16:26,369
比如说歌剧
Things like the opera...

332
00:16:27,498 --> 00:16:29,295
BBC广播3台
...Radio 3...

333
00:16:30,778 --> 00:16:33,338
英国乡间 法律
...the countryside... the law...

334
00:16:34,338 --> 00:16:36,374
还有大学
...the universities.

335
00:16:36,538 --> 00:16:38,529
两所都算 (牛津和剑桥)
Both of them.

336
00:16:41,058 --> 00:16:44,334
而我们就是这个体制         天啊
And we are that system.        Gosh!

337
00:16:44,498 --> 00:16:48,491
我们运作一个文明的 贵族的政府机器
We run a civilised, aristocratic government machine

338
00:16:48,658 --> 00:16:51,616
偶尔由普选调节一下
tempered by occasional general elections.

339
00:16:53,058 --> 00:16:56,304
从1832年议会改革起 我们已经逐渐
Since 1832, we have been gradually

340
00:16:56,305 --> 00:16:58,451
将普通选民排除出政府系统
excluding the voter from government.

341
00:16:58,618 --> 00:17:00,615
现在我们已经达到了
Now we've got them to a point

342
00:17:00,616 --> 00:17:03,009
只让他们每5年选举一次的地步
where they just vote once every five years

343
00:17:03,178 --> 00:17:05,136
还是有些小丑利用这个途径
for which buffoons will try to

344
00:17:05,137 --> 00:17:06,648
干涉我们的政策
interfere with OUR policies

345
00:17:06,818 --> 00:17:09,537
而你倒很乐意把这一切都抛弃?
and you are happy to see all that thrown away?

346
00:17:09,698 --> 00:17:11,654
不不 我不是说...
Well, no, no, I didn't mean...

347
00:17:11,818 --> 00:17:13,973
伯纳 你愿意看到湖区
Bernard, do you want the Lake District

348
00:17:13,974 --> 00:17:16,812
变成一大片房车营地吗?
turned into a gigantic caravan site?

349
00:17:17,818 --> 00:17:22,016
皇家歌剧院变成赌场大厅呢?
The Royal Opera House into a bingo hall?

350
00:17:23,018 --> 00:17:27,216
国家剧院变成地毯超市呢?
The National Theatre into a carpet sale warehouse?

351
00:17:27,378 --> 00:17:29,608
其实看上去挺像的
Well, it looks like one, actually.

352
00:17:31,898 --> 00:17:34,010
我们给设计师封了爵士
We gave the architect a knighthood

353
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:35,891
就是为了不让人这么说
so that nobody would ever say that.

354
00:17:39,658 --> 00:17:45,449
你愿意广播3台全天播流行音乐吗?
Do you want Radio 3 to broadcast pop music 24 hours a day?

355
00:17:45,618 --> 00:17:46,546
要是他们把电视上
How would you feel

356
00:17:46,547 --> 00:17:49,611
所有文化节目都取消 你什么感觉?
if they took all the culture programmes off television?

357
00:17:49,778 --> 00:17:50,970
我不知道 我从来不看
I never watch them.

358
00:17:50,971 --> 00:17:54,090
我也不看 但它们的存在至关重要
Neither do I, but it's vital to know they're there!

359
00:17:54,978 --> 00:17:58,175
可您说地方政府腐败无能的
You said local government was corrupt and incompetent.

360
00:17:58,338 --> 00:17:59,232
确实如此 伯纳
So it is, Bernard.

361
00:17:59,233 --> 00:18:04,334
已经腐败无能到连大臣们都看出来了
So corrupt and incompetent that even ministers recognise it.

362
00:18:04,498 --> 00:18:07,092
这就意味着它们集中了
Which means that they centralise.

363
00:18:07,258 --> 00:18:11,092
所有的实务都交给了我们
They give all the responsible jobs to us.

364
00:18:11,258 --> 00:18:15,456
我们是...政府之中的花朵 伯纳
We... are the flower of government, Bernard.

365
00:18:16,298 --> 00:18:19,096
地方政府尽管是粪土堆
Local government may be a dunghill...

366
00:18:20,378 --> 00:18:23,768
但它们能培育出美丽的玫瑰
...but it grows beautiful roses.

367
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:26,775
您是说...
You mean...

368
00:18:28,098 --> 00:18:30,214
是的 没错 伯纳
Yes, that's right, Bernard.

369
00:18:30,378 --> 00:18:34,371
但如果我们试着清除粪土堆
But if we try to clean up the dunghill

370
00:18:34,538 --> 00:18:38,133
不小心失去了平衡
and... lose our balance...

371
00:18:38,298 --> 00:18:42,086
我们就要摔在...      谢谢 伯纳
We land in the...      Thank you, Bernard.

372
00:18:45,178 --> 00:18:47,487
有劳你了 谢谢
That's very good of you. Thank you.

373
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:52,768
你可以理解我的担忧吧 阿诺德
So you see why I'm so worried, Arnold.

374
00:18:52,938 --> 00:18:55,214
这个马里奥计划是个导火索
This Marriott scheme is the thin end of the wedge.

375
00:18:55,215 --> 00:18:58,331
它最终会侵蚀到公务员系统
It could eventually undermine the Civil Service.

376
00:18:58,498 --> 00:19:01,452
我不觉得有那么危险
Oh, I don't think there's any danger of that.

377
00:19:01,453 --> 00:19:03,014
你运用得法就不会
Not if you play it right.

378
00:19:04,338 --> 00:19:07,171
哈克只是在抓救命稻草
Hacker's just grasping at straws.

379
00:19:07,338 --> 00:19:08,994
这是个古老的逻辑悖论
It's the old logical fallacy.

380
00:19:08,995 --> 00:19:12,571
猫都有4条腿 我的狗也有4条腿
All cats have four legs. My dog has four legs...

381
00:19:13,578 --> 00:19:16,138
因此我的狗是只猫
Therefore my dog is a cat.

382
00:19:17,338 --> 00:19:20,057
政客逻辑害了他
He's suffering from politician's logic.

383
00:19:20,218 --> 00:19:23,051
必须做实事 这是实事 因此必须做
Something must be done therefore we must do it.

384
00:19:23,218 --> 00:19:26,415
可如果做错了 还不如不做
But doing the wrong thing is worse than doing nothing.

385
00:19:26,578 --> 00:19:29,297
做什么都不如什么都不做
Doing anything is worse than doing nothing.

386
00:19:29,898 --> 00:19:32,319
对 毕竟 唯一一件能让政治家
After all, what is the one thing that obsesses

387
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:34,926
追求一生的是什么?
politicians throughout their careers?

388
00:19:35,098 --> 00:19:38,107
很显然是曝光度和支持率
Well, obviously publicity and popularity.

389
00:19:38,108 --> 00:19:40,047
报纸上登个名 电视上露个脸
Name in the paper, face on the telly.

390
00:19:40,218 --> 00:19:43,210
任何能帮他们赢得选举的东西      很对
Anything to help get them re elected.        Quite.

391
00:19:43,378 --> 00:19:46,393
执政党意味着名声 荣耀 显赫
Government is fame and glory and importance

392
00:19:46,394 --> 00:19:48,577
还有超大办公室和司机
and big offices and chauffeurs

393
00:19:48,738 --> 00:19:51,730
还有特里-沃根的专访
and being interviewed by Terry Wogan.

394
00:19:53,098 --> 00:19:56,693
而在野党则是无足轻重 无关紧要的
Opposition is impotence and insignificance

395
00:19:56,858 --> 00:20:00,168
别人都问你是不是认识罗宾-戴
and people at parties asking you if you know Robin Day.

396
00:20:00,898 --> 00:20:05,501
但是 阿诺德 公务员体系改革
But, Arnold, reforming the Civil Service

397
00:20:05,502 --> 00:20:07,212
也许能为他们赢得民心
might win them popularity.

398
00:20:08,018 --> 00:20:11,408
但这是不可能的 是吧 汉弗莱?
But it can't ever happen... can it, Humphrey?

399
00:20:12,418 --> 00:20:16,252
怎么不能 阿诺德?         这跟地方政府是一样的
Why not, Arnold?      It's the same as in local government.

400
00:20:16,418 --> 00:20:17,949
6万人的大选区
Constituencies of 60,000 are

401
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:20,889
选民注定无法了解他们的议会代表
far too big for people to know their MP.

402
00:20:21,058 --> 00:20:23,207
选民们作出决定的基础是
Electors make up their minds on the basis

403
00:20:23,208 --> 00:20:25,654
广播电视和媒体的宣传
of the telly and the radio and the press.

404
00:20:25,818 --> 00:20:28,616
是的 他们选出他们最喜欢的党派领袖
Yes, they pick their favourite party leader,

405
00:20:28,778 --> 00:20:30,044
就等于投票给那党派中
then they vote for whatever clown

406
00:20:30,044 --> 00:20:32,582
一小撮人指定的
a few people in their party

407
00:20:32,582 --> 00:20:34,569
随便什么下三滥候选人
have chosen as their candidate.

408
00:20:34,738 --> 00:20:38,328
相信我 我了解这个体制 阿诺德
I do understand how the system works, Arnold.

409
00:20:38,329 --> 00:20:39,175
但你真的了解吗?
But do you?

410
00:20:39,898 --> 00:20:43,303
汉弗莱 如果一个政客的生死
Listen, Humphrey, if a politician lives or dies

411
00:20:43,304 --> 00:20:45,052
由他的媒体形象决定
by his media image,

412
00:20:45,218 --> 00:20:49,052
那他的生存就取决于公务员公关系统
then his survival depends on the Civil Service publicity machine

413
00:20:49,218 --> 00:20:51,558
来润色他愚蠢的讲话稿
helping him with his fatuous speeches

414
00:20:51,559 --> 00:20:56,090
写的文章 还有媒体出镜
and articles and photo opportunities.

415
00:20:56,258 --> 00:20:58,977
政客们完全依靠我们
Politicians are dependent on us.

416
00:20:59,138 --> 00:21:03,529
上千名新闻官员 鼓吹他们那点小政绩
A thousand press officers to publicise their little triumphs.

417
00:21:03,698 --> 00:21:08,294
<官方保密法> 掩盖他们每天的丑闻
The Official Secrets Act to conceal their daily disasters.

418
00:21:09,178 --> 00:21:12,966
那么你是说 按马里奥教授的计划
So what you're saying is that under Professor Marriott's scheme,

419
00:21:13,138 --> 00:21:16,110
议员会凭他们在地方上的声望当选
MPs would be elected on their local reputation

420
00:21:16,111 --> 00:21:18,576
而不是党派领袖的媒体形象
rather than on their leader's media image.

421
00:21:18,738 --> 00:21:22,731
对 政府和大臣们就得去挣选票
Yes, governments and ministers would have to earn their votes.

422
00:21:22,898 --> 00:21:25,202
真的做选民们希望的事
Actually do what the electors want

423
00:21:25,203 --> 00:21:27,210
而不是让我们按我们的方法做事
instead of leaving us to do it our way

424
00:21:27,378 --> 00:21:29,369
他们只管树立形象就成
while they do the fame and glory bit.

425
00:21:30,258 --> 00:21:31,976
想想都可怕
Frightening thought.

426
00:21:32,898 --> 00:21:36,208
对我们可怕 但对首相呢?
Frightening to us, but what about the Prime Minister?

427
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:41,566
自然是更可怕了
Of course. Even more frightening.

428
00:21:41,738 --> 00:21:43,600
公务员改革就等于撤除了
Reforming the Civil Service would remove

429
00:21:43,601 --> 00:21:45,447
他的生命线
his life support system.

430
00:21:46,578 --> 00:21:49,968
等于抽掉他一路爬上来的梯子
It would kick away the ladder that's put him where he is.

431
00:21:50,138 --> 00:21:53,050
而且他还站在上面呢
While he's still standing on it.

432
00:21:53,778 --> 00:21:55,769
非常正确
That's right.

433
00:21:55,938 --> 00:21:58,597
改革公务员系统的唯一方法
The only way to reform the Civil Service system

434
00:21:58,598 --> 00:22:01,058
就是把政治体制一起改掉
is to reform the political system.

435
00:22:01,218 --> 00:22:02,936
没有哪个政府会改掉
No government's going to reform

436
00:22:02,937 --> 00:22:05,211
赋与其权力的体制吧
the system that put it into power.

437
00:22:07,138 --> 00:22:10,926
问题是 要让首相也看到危险
The thing is to get the Prime Minister to see the danger.

438
00:22:11,098 --> 00:22:13,089
这是你的事
That's your job.

439
00:22:14,098 --> 00:22:15,878
有了
I know.

440
00:22:15,879 --> 00:22:19,570
我跟他说 这会是他最有魄力的举措
I'll tell him it'll be the most courageous thing he's ever done.

441
00:22:21,698 --> 00:22:23,893
这招百发百中
That always does the trick.

442
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:27,413
进来
Yes?

443
00:22:27,578 --> 00:22:29,910
艾格尼丝-莫豪来了 汉弗莱爵士
Agnes Moorhouse, Sir Humphrey.

444
00:22:29,911 --> 00:22:31,776
艾格尼丝
Ah, Agnes.

445
00:22:31,938 --> 00:22:33,929
请这边坐
Why don't you sit over here?

446
00:22:36,418 --> 00:22:39,742
艾格尼丝 首相非常担忧
Agnes, the Prime Minister's really worried about

447
00:22:39,743 --> 00:22:41,253
你对警察队伍的态度
your attitude to the police.

448
00:22:41,418 --> 00:22:43,010
哦 很好
Oh, good.

449
00:22:43,978 --> 00:22:49,575
因此 他计划全盘改造地方政府
So he's proposing a wholesale reform of local government.

450
00:22:50,298 --> 00:22:54,257
街道代表 每200户选一个
Street representatives, voting communities of 200 households,

451
00:22:54,418 --> 00:22:56,752
让他们全面参与自制市镇
total involvement of the borough electorate

452
00:22:56,753 --> 00:22:59,412
总代表候选人的提名
in the selection of candidates.

453
00:22:59,578 --> 00:23:02,615
不是真的吧?          恐怕是的
This isn't serious?        Oh, I'm afraid it is.

454
00:23:04,698 --> 00:23:08,293
这会重创我们的民主社会改革啊
This strikes at the heart of our democratic social reforms.

455
00:23:08,458 --> 00:23:12,770
你是说 人们其实不喜欢你的政策?
Do you mean the people don't want your policies?

456
00:23:12,938 --> 00:23:15,888
他们要是能理解 当然会喜欢
Of course they would if they could understand,

457
00:23:15,889 --> 00:23:18,934
可普通选民都头脑简单
but the ordinary voters are simple people.

458
00:23:19,098 --> 00:23:20,654
他们看不到自己的需求
They don't see their needs.

459
00:23:20,655 --> 00:23:22,693
他们不会分析问题
They can't analyse problems.

460
00:23:22,858 --> 00:23:25,577
他们得跟着领袖 才能往该走的方向走
They need leadership to guide them the way they ought to go.

461
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:29,617
你觉得"人民"不会投票给这种领袖?
And don't you think "the people" would vote for such leadership?

462
00:23:29,778 --> 00:23:31,675
人民并不总能分清好歹
People don't always understand what's good for them.

463
00:23:31,676 --> 00:23:36,729
哦 我太同意你了
Oh... I do so agree with you.

464
00:23:37,418 --> 00:23:39,613
是吗?      当然了
Do you?      Of course!

465
00:23:39,778 --> 00:23:43,771
这就是公务员系统传承几个世纪的原因
That's how the Civil Service has survived for centuries.

466
00:23:43,938 --> 00:23:46,007
我们造就了这个国家
We made this country what it is,

467
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:48,216
可没人会投票给我们
but nobody would ever vote for us!

468
00:23:48,898 --> 00:23:51,229
我们清楚什么对国家有好处
We know what's right for this country!

469
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:52,368
可不是吗
So do we!

470
00:23:52,538 --> 00:23:54,814
唯一办法就是 只选一小群领导人
The only way is to have a small group in charge

471
00:23:54,815 --> 00:23:57,453
让人民隔几年投一次票
and let the people have a vote every few years.

472
00:23:57,618 --> 00:24:00,451
如果他们对候选人了解太深
If they knew the people they were voting for...

473
00:24:00,618 --> 00:24:02,182
如果让他们说上话
If they actually talked to them,

474
00:24:02,183 --> 00:24:05,214
他们都会迷上那些老一套的蠢办法
they'd fall for all the silly conventional ideas!

475
00:24:06,098 --> 00:24:08,293
汉弗莱           艾格尼丝?
Humphrey...        Agnes?

476
00:24:10,058 --> 00:24:12,492
这对你也是个灾难 你知道吗?
This would be a disaster for you, too. you know?

477
00:24:12,658 --> 00:24:14,569
我知道
I know.

478
00:24:14,738 --> 00:24:18,128
社区委员会最终会形成地区政府
Community councils always lead to regional government.

479
00:24:18,298 --> 00:24:22,257
艾格尼丝 我们必须阻止首相
Agnes... we must stop the Prime Minister!

480
00:24:23,178 --> 00:24:24,549
你也想阻止他?
You want to stop him, too?

481
00:24:24,550 --> 00:24:26,966
当然 而你得帮我
Of course. And you must help me.

482
00:24:27,138 --> 00:24:30,733
怎么帮?           我想我知道要怎么做
How?        Well, I think I know how to do it.

483
00:24:30,898 --> 00:24:33,107
但我要你书面保证
But I want your written assurance

484
00:24:33,108 --> 00:24:35,130
不再骚扰你的地方警察局
that you will stop harassing your local police.

485
00:24:35,298 --> 00:24:39,610
我是说 不再让他们民主地对你负责
I mean, stop making them democratically accountable to you.

486
00:24:39,778 --> 00:24:41,769
这可以把事态缓和一下
It will remove some of the urgency.

487
00:24:43,178 --> 00:24:46,011
好的 你要我怎么说?
Right. What do you want me to say?

488
00:24:46,178 --> 00:24:48,169
这个 我觉得
Well, I thought...

489
00:24:49,338 --> 00:24:51,932
就像这些之类
it might go something like this.

490
00:24:57,218 --> 00:24:59,493
哦 汉弗莱
Oh, Humphrey...

491
00:25:00,498 --> 00:25:03,251
你不参加激进运动真让人痛心
...you're a great loss to the militant revolution.

492
00:25:04,938 --> 00:25:06,929
而你 亲爱的艾格尼丝
And you, my dear Agnes...

493
00:25:08,018 --> 00:25:10,816
不加入公务员也让人痛心
...are a great loss to the Civil Service.

494
00:25:18,378 --> 00:25:21,061
为什么汉弗莱要我亲自见见马里奥?
Why does Humphrey want me to see Marriott?

495
00:25:21,062 --> 00:25:22,530
他肯定有见不得人的计划
He must have an ulterior motive.

496
00:25:22,698 --> 00:25:23,358
为什么?
Why?

497
00:25:23,359 --> 00:25:26,247
汉弗莱所有计划都见不得人
All Humphrey's motives are ulterior.

498
00:25:26,418 --> 00:25:27,770
是吗 伯纳?
Has he, Bernard?

499
00:25:27,771 --> 00:25:30,411
汉弗莱对这计划到底什么看法?
What does Humphrey really think about this plan?

500
00:25:30,578 --> 00:25:32,773
这个 呃 我想...
Well, er... Well, I think...

501
00:25:32,938 --> 00:25:35,930
我肯定 如果您真的决心...
That is, I'm sure, if it's what you want...

502
00:25:36,098 --> 00:25:38,692
我相信汉弗莱爵士一定会...
I'm sure Sir Humphrey would...

503
00:25:38,858 --> 00:25:41,736
一定会...           有这么糟?
He would... er...        As bad as that?

504
00:25:42,698 --> 00:25:45,015
首相 马里奥教授来了
Professor Marriott is outside.

505
00:25:45,015 --> 00:25:45,515
您要见他吗?
Will you see him?

506
00:25:45,516 --> 00:25:46,486
好 当然了
Yes, of course.

507
00:25:46,658 --> 00:25:48,210
伯纳 能不能请你...
Bernard, I wonder if you'd be kind enough.

508
00:25:48,211 --> 00:25:52,369
汉弗莱 你对马里奥的计划有何看法?
What's your view of the Marriott plan?

509
00:25:52,538 --> 00:25:54,963
我觉得 它能顺利把真正的民主
It is a brilliant way of bringing real democracy

510
00:25:54,964 --> 00:25:56,531
引入英国政府
into the government of Britain.

511
00:25:56,698 --> 00:26:00,293
所以你支持?        他没这么说
So you're in favour?        That's not what he said.

512
00:26:00,458 --> 00:26:03,814
首相 如果你想要一个真正民主的政府
If you want real democratic government,

513
00:26:03,815 --> 00:26:06,055
我定当鼎力支持
you will have my unquestioning support.

514
00:26:06,765 --> 00:26:08,550
马里奥教授来了
Professor Marriott.

515
00:26:08,550 --> 00:26:12,648
教授 请进 多谢光临 请坐
Professor, come in. Good of you to come. Do sit down.

516
00:26:12,818 --> 00:26:14,491
首相 见到您太荣幸了
What an honour to meet you.

517
00:26:14,492 --> 00:26:16,015
对 我知道
Yes, I know.

518
00:26:17,938 --> 00:26:22,175
首相 马里奥教授又写了篇续作
Professor Marriott has a sequel to his original article

519
00:26:22,176 --> 00:26:23,410
将要在下月出版
that's due to be published next month.

520
00:26:23,578 --> 00:26:26,775
比原作还要激动人心
It is even more exciting than the first one.

521
00:26:26,938 --> 00:26:27,972
跟我说说吧 教授
Tell me more, Professor.

522
00:26:27,973 --> 00:26:31,773
是呀 跟首相说说它对议会的好处
Tell the PM about the benefits to Parliament.

523
00:26:31,938 --> 00:26:35,533
如您所知 按照我的地方政府方案
Well, as you know, under my local government scheme,

524
00:26:35,698 --> 00:26:39,976
每个市镇有500名街道代表
each borough would have its 500 street representatives.

525
00:26:40,138 --> 00:26:42,154
这意味着当地议员可以
This means the local MP would be

526
00:26:42,155 --> 00:26:44,318
在一个大厅里同他们交流
able to talk to them all in one hall.

527
00:26:44,318 --> 00:26:46,294
让他们了解他
They'd get to know him.

528
00:26:46,294 --> 00:26:48,694
正是 然后回去讲给左邻右舍听
And tell all the people in their street about him.

529
00:26:48,695 --> 00:26:51,215
面对面 树立口碑
Word of mouth recommendation.

530
00:26:51,378 --> 00:26:52,330
听起来真好
Sounds terrific.

531
00:26:52,331 --> 00:26:56,054
等等 那参选党派起什么作用?
Where would the constituency party come in?

532
00:26:56,218 --> 00:26:58,209
这就是妙处所在
Ah, that's the marvellous thing.

533
00:26:58,378 --> 00:27:01,848
党派完全成了摆设了
Party organisations would be completely bypassed.

534
00:27:02,018 --> 00:27:05,727
议员们将真正独立出来      什么?
MPs would become genuinely independent.        What?

535
00:27:05,898 --> 00:27:09,421
如果候选人被所有委员会代表
If they were known to all their constituents

536
00:27:09,422 --> 00:27:10,892
所有选民所了解
or their committee representatives,

537
00:27:11,058 --> 00:27:14,400
赢得选举将不再取决于
then getting re elected would be nothing to do with

538
00:27:14,401 --> 00:27:16,007
党派是否支持他们
whether the party backed them or not

539
00:27:16,178 --> 00:27:19,727
而取决于选民觉得他干得怎样
but on whether the constituents felt they were doing a good job.

540
00:27:19,898 --> 00:27:22,890
所以 如果议员们不再依赖党派
If the MP wasn't dependent on his party machine,

541
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:26,209
他就尽可以投票反对自己党派的政策
he could vote against his own party and get away with it.

542
00:27:26,378 --> 00:27:28,369
候选人不再由官方指定
There'd be no official candidates.

543
00:27:28,538 --> 00:27:32,138
选举结果完全取决于候选人的名声
Election would depend on an MP's reputation,

544
00:27:32,139 --> 00:27:34,135
而不是党派领袖的形象
not the image of the party leader.

545
00:27:34,298 --> 00:27:38,086
政党机器就完了 组织秘书也完了
An end of the party machine. An end to the power of the whips.

546
00:27:38,258 --> 00:27:39,375
那政府要怎样让它
How would the government gets

547
00:27:39,376 --> 00:27:43,651
不受欢迎的法案顺利通过呢?
its unpopular legislation through without twisting the odd arm?

548
00:27:43,818 --> 00:27:46,412
少数怎样指使多数?        不行
How would it command a majority?        It couldn't.

549
00:27:46,578 --> 00:27:47,939
一项法案要通过
There could only be legislation

550
00:27:47,940 --> 00:27:51,777
得有多数议员支持才行
if a majority of the MPs were actually in favour of it.

551
00:27:51,938 --> 00:27:54,611
议会将真正民主起来
Parliament would become genuinely democratic.

552
00:27:54,778 --> 00:27:58,605
首相 这是您所提议过的
Prime Minister, it is the most courageous policy

553
00:27:58,606 --> 00:28:00,614
最有魄力的方案
you have ever proposed.

554
00:28:02,858 --> 00:28:06,055
教授 非常感谢 太妙了 再见
Professor, thank you so much. Fascinating. Goodbye.

555
00:28:08,578 --> 00:28:10,967
谢谢您 首相
Thank you, Prime Minister.

556
00:28:11,138 --> 00:28:13,572
首相 真宏伟的计划啊
Prime Minister, it's a splendid idea.

557
00:28:13,738 --> 00:28:16,775
真正的民主      多萝西 这根本不能考虑
Real democracy.        It's out of the question.

558
00:28:16,938 --> 00:28:18,592
马里奥的计划应该是我们
The Marriott scheme was our way

559
00:28:18,593 --> 00:28:20,931
用来控制地方政府的
of controlling the local authority.

560
00:28:21,098 --> 00:28:23,359
现在怎么对付莫豪的警察问题?
What will we do about Agnes Moorhouse?

561
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:26,297
首相 我又跟她谈了一次
I've had another word with her.

562
00:28:26,458 --> 00:28:28,738
简而言之 首相
To put it simply, Prime Minister,

563
00:28:28,739 --> 00:28:31,248
我们进行了一番非正式讨论
certain informal discussions took place

564
00:28:31,418 --> 00:28:34,096
全面而坦率地交换了意见
involving a full and frank exchange of views,

565
00:28:34,097 --> 00:28:37,015
从而提出了一系列计划
out of which there arose a series of proposals

566
00:28:37,178 --> 00:28:40,887
最终引导了多种可行的研究目标
which proved to indicate certain promising lines of inquiry,

567
00:28:41,058 --> 00:28:42,032
依此推进之后
which, when pursued,

568
00:28:42,033 --> 00:28:45,848
得出结论 有某些其它方案
led to the realisation that the alternative courses of action

569
00:28:46,018 --> 00:28:47,818
也许在某种情况下
might, in fact, in certain circumstances,

570
00:28:47,819 --> 00:28:50,614
能对既定方针作出谨慎补充
be susceptible of discreet modification,

571
00:28:50,778 --> 00:28:53,770
以实现求同存异
leading to a reappraisal of the areas of difference

572
00:28:53,938 --> 00:28:55,848
寻找一条途径 使双方有条件
and pointing the way to encouraging possibilities

573
00:28:55,849 --> 00:28:58,728
妥协接受并通力合作
of compromise and cooperation

574
00:28:58,898 --> 00:29:00,808
如果双方都能贯彻执行
which, if bilaterally implemented

575
00:29:00,809 --> 00:29:03,096
并同时作出适当的让步
with appropriate give and take on both sides,

576
00:29:03,258 --> 00:29:05,099
若形势许可 也许会
might, if the climate were right,

577
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:07,251
最终创造出可能条件
have a possibility, at the end of the day,

578
00:29:07,418 --> 00:29:09,395
无论过程正确与否 都能达成
of leading, rightly or wrongly,

579
00:29:09,396 --> 00:29:11,809
双方均满意的解决方案
to a mutually satisfactory resolution.

580
00:29:14,378 --> 00:29:16,846
你在扯什么啊?
What the hell are you talking about?

581
00:29:19,218 --> 00:29:21,209
我们做了笔交易
We did a deal.

582
00:29:23,538 --> 00:29:25,195
果不其然
Oddly enough,

583
00:29:25,196 --> 00:29:28,328
她对民主的欲望并不比您强
she didn't seem to like the idea of democracy any more than you.

584
00:29:28,498 --> 00:29:31,331
或者你     非常对 亲爱的女士
Or you.        Quite so, dear lady.

585
00:29:31,498 --> 00:29:33,189
我想我们都同意
Well, I think we're all agreed

586
00:29:33,190 --> 00:29:34,759
国家还没准备好
that the nation isn't quite ready for

587
00:29:34,759 --> 00:29:36,305
迎接完全的民主
total democracy.

588
00:29:37,378 --> 00:29:39,494
也许要到...下个世纪?
Perhaps... er... next century?

589
00:29:40,818 --> 00:29:44,606
可能下个世纪 您还是首相
Well, you could still be Prime Minister next century.

590
00:29:45,498 --> 00:29:48,456
那就下下世纪      是 首相
Well, the one after that.        Yes, Prime Minister.

591
00:29:51,100 --> 00:30:01,570
